        {
          "kind": "Function",
          "canonicalReference": "@ory/tanstack-start!oryProxyMiddleware:function(1)",
          "docComment": "/**\n * Creates request middleware that serves Ory's APIs on the app's own origin, so Ory's cookies are first-party during local development and on preview deployments. In production, use a custom domain on Ory Network, or your own domain with the Ory Enterprise License: through the proxy, Ory sees your server as the client instead of your users.\n *\n * Register it after Start's CSRF middleware. Once `src/start.ts` defines a `startInstance`, Start no longer adds its default CSRF middleware.\n *\n * @param options - The proxy options. `trustedOrigins` is required.\n *\n * @returns The request middleware.\n *\n * @example\n * ```ts\n * // src/start.ts\n * import { oryProxyMiddleware } from \"@ory/tanstack-start/proxy\"\n * import { createCsrfMiddleware, createStart } from \"@tanstack/react-start\"\n *\n * const csrfMiddleware = createCsrfMiddleware({\n *   filter: (ctx) => ctx.handlerType === \"serverFn\",\n * })\n *\n * const oryProxy = oryProxyMiddleware({\n *   trustedOrigins: [\"http://localhost:3000\"],\n * })\n *\n * export const startInstance = createStart(() => ({\n *   requestMiddleware: [csrfMiddleware, oryProxy],\n * }))\n * ```\n *\n * @throws\n *\n * TypeError when `trustedOrigins` is empty or has an invalid entry.\n *\n * @public\n */\n",
          "excerptTokens": [
